Notebook[{
Cell["Tropical Algebra of ReLU Networks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"6d8ce032-189a-4042-ae9b-4c4f680ea2b1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A ReLU neural network is literally a tropical rational map.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " This post takes that statement seriously and turns it into a working \
computational essay. We start with the max-plus semiring on its own terms -- \
defining the operators, building tropical matrices, running shortest-path and \
project-scheduling algorithms entirely inside the algebra -- and only then \
cross over to neural networks. By the end, we will have rewritten a trained \
ReLU classifier as a difference of two tropical polynomials, visualised its \
decision boundary as a tropical hypersurface, and used the tropical lens to \
derive three results that go beyond the standard literature: a much sharper, \
region-enumerated Lipschitz constant; a ",
 StyleBox["zero-data",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " detector for ",
 StyleBox["dead",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " neurons on any bounded input domain; and a ",
 StyleBox["zero-retraining network pruner",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that is provably exact on the chosen domain."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"27cad8eb-fedb-4893-bfa5-26e56935ddf6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every code block below is executable Wolfram Language. The cells have been \
pre-evaluated so the published notebook is self-contained: the reader sees \
both the code and its result without having to evaluate anything. Companion \
repository: ",
 StyleBox["github.com/mthiel74/TropicalAlgebravsReLU",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f51ba8e3-8038-4fbf-9767-ebb2caa08389"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To re-evaluate the cells yourself in a fresh kernel, place the two \
companion packages ",
 StyleBox["MaxPlus.wl",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["TropicalReLU.wl",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 " (downloadable from the repository above) in the ",
 StyleBox["same directory as this notebook",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and evaluate the cell below. Every analytical tool used later in the post \
-- ",
 StyleBox["TropicalPolynomial",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["TropicalEval",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["MPSchedule",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["MPCycleMean",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["MPLinearSystemEvolve",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["TropicalDecomposition",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["MPExactLipschitz",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["MPDeadUnits",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["MPPruneDeadUnits",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 " -- is defined in those two files."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8e25f44e-cb23-48fc-b6d9-576fba734134"],

Cell["\<\
SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];
Get[\"MaxPlus.wl\"];
Get[\"TropicalReLU.wl\"];
Needs[\"MaxPlus`\"];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4e738ea2-0487-4b56-92bf-a9aa529b159d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Primary reference: L. Zhang, G. Naitzat, L.-H. Lim, ",
 StyleBox["Tropical Geometry of Deep Neural Networks",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ICML 2018 (arXiv:1805.07091).  This essay extends their picture with \
concrete WL implementations of the standard tropical machinery \
(Maclagan-Sturmfels, Butkovic) and with the analytical tools in \[Section]18 \
that follow naturally from the tropical viewpoint but are not in the ICML \
paper."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6c9f77b2-b045-4ef6-a992-46d0fe658968"],

