Cell["\<\
Two windows on two algebras. Left: the smooth, continuous world of classical \
arithmetic (R, +, *). Right: the same landscape under (max, +) -- every \
operation produces a crisp polyhedral surface. The two are connected by a \
small bridge.\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"6aed58d9-1d61-4a83-a3ef-0af7ecd38989"],

Cell["1.  The max-plus semiring in 60 seconds", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"509e4a43-3d01-4a33-b339-f5ca1cf5a86b"],

Cell["\<\
The tropical (max-plus) semiring is the set of real numbers extended with \
negative infinity,\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0ed2fe39-d43b-4cdf-98d0-3026ee77b626"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SubscriptBox["R", "max"], "=", 
  RowBox[{"R", "\[Union]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}], "}"}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"4d0a6d3b-193a-4a51-ba52-234ce3542293"],

Cell["\<\
equipped with two operations that look like the addition and multiplication \
of classical algebra but are:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06042a13-8208-4c9c-a37d-033537ac34f4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "\[CirclePlus]", "b"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{"max", "(", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], ")"}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"071ff118-936f-4886-b56f-60dc22e5bcf2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "\[CircleTimes]", "b"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{"a", "+", "b"}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"a6bed5e7-143f-4c38-9067-8e95ef724eb5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The identities flip: the additive identity is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "67202307-37e4-4f43-9b1c-b4bbb7e57d8e"],
 " (since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"max", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}], ",", "a"}], ")"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cd457bfa-18f1-49ab-92ff-e65f05733fd3"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["a",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ca26733f-1a2c-480a-adf9-749a90f8a353"],
 "), and the multiplicative identity is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["0",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "dbf94389-f0e3-4f55-b0bd-0f8f55086995"],
 " (since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"0", "+", "a"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5c2910e1-b1eb-4a04-a33f-e0f9916b51bb"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["a",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "43d74b24-d0fc-4efe-879f-999287a7d5bd"],
 "). Apart from the absence of additive inverses (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     SubscriptBox["R", "\"\<max\>\""],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ae565db6-6b11-48c7-8bca-7af195b1cb86"],
 " is a semiring, not a ring), every familiar axiom of a commutative ring \
carries over. Distributivity in particular: "
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"75253f89-cd3c-418b-a48b-ec22df34d736"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a", "\[CircleTimes]", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"b", "\[CirclePlus]", "c"}], ")"}]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "\[CircleTimes]", "b"}], "\[CirclePlus]", 
      RowBox[{"a", "\[CircleTimes]", "c"}]}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"0db40717-eaf3-403d-b675-b79e04c0d215"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is worth pausing on what this re-labelling really buys you. Classical \
addition and multiplication are continuous and smooth, whereas ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["Max",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2980cfae-1fda-4af0-b258-8f08ae961193"],
 " has a non-differentiable corner. So every identity of ordinary algebra \
translates into an identity about piecewise-linear convex functions. \
Polynomials become piecewise-linear functions. Powers become repeated \
max-with-translation. The distributive law becomes the statement that ",
 StyleBox["a classical sum of convex piecewise-linear functions is again a \
convex piecewise-linear function",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " -- a deeply non-obvious fact in ordinary analysis, but a trivial \
consequence of the semiring axioms once you have the right operator names. \
This is the lever the rest of the post pulls on."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c480d69e-b950-49a3-8220-2e496be0ae1d"],

Cell["Why 'tropical'?", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"14335e07-0836-4ff1-944a-4a26f1dc05b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The name was coined in the 1980s by French computer scientists -- most \
often attributed to Christian Choffrut, working in the circle of Dominique \
Perrin, Jean-\[CapitalEAcute]ric Pin, and Marcel-Paul \
Sch\[UDoubleDot]tzenberger -- in honour of Imre Simon, a Brazilian-Hungarian \
mathematician (born in Budapest 1943, emigrated to Brazil after the 1956 \
revolution, professor at IME-USP) who pioneered the use of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     SubscriptBox["R", "\"\<max\>\""],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e9a9fe84-d817-44a4-b613-41b391f6fd15"],
 " semiring in formal language theory. There is no deeper geometric meaning \
-- 'tropical' is simply a tribute to where Simon worked. The algebra itself \
is as old as ",
 StyleBox["operations research",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": Bellman's dynamic-programming recurrences from the 1950s are implicit \
max-plus matrix-vector products. What is new is the use of the tropical lens \
in ",
 StyleBox["neural networks",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", which is the thread we will follow."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c89d4f42-8990-4772-8823-a4bef0da240a"],

Cell["Idempotence: a new identity", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"c70187ba-2019-4fc0-acd5-e55c0ae55166"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One identity of classical algebra is conspicuously ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " inherited: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "+", "a"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "a"}]}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5c2299b4-e523-4e73-afa7-1cd2e53e8bd2"],
 " has no tropical analogue, because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "\[CirclePlus]", "a"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
      RowBox[{"max", "(", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", "a"}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "a"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "401adf8b-1d92-4571-9e83-994673c2bb3f"],
 ". The tropical sum of anything with itself is itself. This is the ",
 StyleBox["idempotence",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " axiom, and it is the algebraic shadow of the fact that the maximum of a \
set does not change when you repeat its elements. A small numerical check \
makes the asymmetry concrete:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d1e0628-da35-4bb8-93b1-410359775fd4"],

Cell["\<\
(* Side-by-side: same six numerical experiments in both algebras *)
Grid[
  Join[
    {{\"classical\", \"=\", \"tropical\", \"=\", \"reading\"}},
    {
      {\"3 + 5\",  3 + 5,
       \"3 \\[CirclePlus] 5\",  3 \\[CirclePlus] 5,
       \"\\[CirclePlus] picks the larger\"},
      {\"3 \\[Times] 5\", 3 \\[Times] 5,
       \"3 \\[CircleTimes] 5\", 3 \\[CircleTimes] 5,
       \"\\[CircleTimes] is the classical sum\"},
      {\"3 + 3\",  3 + 3,
       \"3 \\[CirclePlus] 3\",  3 \\[CirclePlus] 3,
       \"\\[CirclePlus] is idempotent:  a \\[CirclePlus] a = a\"},
      {\"3 \\[Times] 3\", 3 \\[Times] 3,
       \"3 \\[CircleTimes] 3\", 3 \\[CircleTimes] 3,
       \"powers become repeated translation\"},
      {\"3 + (-\\[Infinity])\", 3 + -Infinity,
       \"3 \\[CirclePlus] (-\\[Infinity])\", 3 \\[CirclePlus] -Infinity,
       \"\\[Minus]\\[Infinity] is the tropical 0\"},
      {\"3 \\[Times] 0\", 3 \\[Times] 0,
       \"3 \\[CircleTimes] 0\", 3 \\[CircleTimes] 0,
       \"0 is the tropical 1\"}
    }
  ],
  Frame -> All, Spacings -> {2, 1.0}, Alignment -> {Left, Center},
  Background -> {None, {1 -> RGBColor[0.18, 0.30, 0.55]}},
  ItemStyle -> {None, {1 -> Directive[White, Bold]}}
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4bced066-2b98-4912-9ca9-7e8a37ec468e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  TagBox[GridBox[{
     {"\<\"classical\"\>", "\<\"=\"\>", "\<\"tropical\"\>", "\<\"=\"\>", \
"\<\"reading\"\>"},
     {"\<\"3 + 5\"\>", "8", "\<\"3 \[CirclePlus] 5\"\>", 
      "5", "\<\"\[CirclePlus] picks the larger\"\>"},
     {"\<\"3 \[Times] 5\"\>", "15", "\<\"3 \[CircleTimes] 5\"\>", 
      "8", "\<\"\[CircleTimes] is the classical sum\"\>"},
     {"\<\"3 + 3\"\>", "6", "\<\"3 \[CirclePlus] 3\"\>", 
      "3", "\<\"\[CirclePlus] is idempotent:  a \[CirclePlus] a = a\"\>"},
     {"\<\"3 \[Times] 3\"\>", "9", "\<\"3 \[CircleTimes] 3\"\>", 
      "6", "\<\"powers become repeated translation\"\>"},
     {"\<\"3 + (-\[Infinity])\"\>", 
      RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}], "\<\"3 \[CirclePlus] (-\[Infinity])\"\>", 
      "3", "\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity] is the tropical 0\"\>"},
     {"\<\"3 \[Times] 0\"\>", "0", "\<\"3 \[CircleTimes] 0\"\>", 
      "3", "\<\"0 is the tropical 1\"\>"}
    },
    AutoDelete->False,
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Center}}},
    GridBoxBackground->{
     "Columns" -> {{None}}, "RowsIndexed" -> {1 -> RGBColor[0.18, 0.3, 0.55]}},
    GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
    GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
    GridBoxItemStyle->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "RowsIndexed" -> {1 -> Directive[
          GrayLevel[1], Bold]}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{2}}, "Rows" -> {{1.}}}],
   "Grid"],
  Alignment->{Center, Top},
  ImageSize->Full]], "Output",
 CellFrame->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"f0069469-b096-469a-ad52-c5f1d2ceb4e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read the rows top-to-bottom. Three is bigger than itself in neither \
algebra: classically ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"3", "+", "3"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d74db44a-8d52-4e65-92ce-41de7d6c5e43"],
 " adds new mass, tropically ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"3", "\[CirclePlus]", "3"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "00da0f76-9227-46e2-a6c8-3009a12de5da"],
 " stays put. The bottom two rows pin down the role of the new identities -- ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "bcd354fb-23f1-4fa5-bf33-1c1cd28c865c"],
 " absorbs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["Max",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c275eba1-8cf6-4660-b0a8-4a1c53067977"],
 " (so it is the \"tropical zero\"), and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["0",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4a2b6fd1-07b5-42ea-8f2e-197523d3a98d"],
 " absorbs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["Plus",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "09bee434-a3ed-456f-a7cc-1e5417c8b5a5"],
 " (so it is the \"tropical one\"). Anyone meeting max-plus for the first \
time will want to hand-evaluate a few rows like these until the swap feels \
natural."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e2964c6-980a-48bc-9e2c-709c7d431d56"],

