  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"f9cfe94c-0c46-4abc-a074-dc1727951572"],

Cell["\<\
A proper tropical rational. Adding more hidden units of the same sign \
tropical-multiplies into P (or Q), doubling the monomial count in the worst \
case.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"41de0a8e-2eb2-4269-92d0-f86536f5eb68"],

Cell["12.  Other tropical-compatible layers", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4ab1a4ab-2ff9-4d17-a5b3-9b1f34e66b2e"],

Cell["\<\
The ReLU \[Rule] tropical correspondence is not a one-off curio. Many \
standard deep-learning building blocks are already tropical:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a20ca464-f806-4d31-b521-f7b983059f89"],

Cell["Leaky ReLU", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"821b0add-1663-4fdd-9386-e0dceb44177c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<LeakyReLU\>\"", "(", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "\[Alpha]"}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{"max", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", "x"}], ",", "x"}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", "x"}], "\[CirclePlus]", "x"}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"2293afc9-ffea-4c67-a272-a44fb71dc2ff"],

Cell["\<\
Two monomials of slopes \[Alpha] and 1; for \[Alpha] in (0, 1) the leaky \
variant simply rotates the negative half of the ReLU off the x-axis. Still a \
degree-1 tropical polynomial.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fc03b049-ad88-4448-9a7f-a66be2b35cec"],

Cell["\<\
LeakyReLU[x_, alpha_] := alpha x \\[CirclePlus] x;
LeakyReLU[#, 0.1] & /@ {-2., -0.5, 0., 0.7, 2.}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b96ed186-9aca-4b94-aabe-7681a7eb0a9b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "0.2`"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "0.05`"}], ",", "0.`", ",", "0.7`", ",", "2.`"}], "}"}],
  Alignment->{Center, Top},
  ImageSize->Full]], "Output",
 CellFrame->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"7ea4f5dd-c6ff-46c2-9ed7-58520e57c9b9"],

Cell["MaxPool", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"9c2e216d-adf0-4506-958e-26f499774348"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Max-pooling over a window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["W",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "452b9993-ff52-4def-94d0-e344cc2cf5fc"],
 " of size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["k",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "36bde154-e443-4b44-adb1-fc59d98cb615"],
 " is, by definition, a tropical sum:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"381039cf-c2dd-4da9-b5f5-e63460acaf69"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<MaxPool\>\"", "(", "x", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["Max", "\"\<i \[Element] W\>\""], " ", 
      SubscriptBox["x", "i"]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["x", 
       SubscriptBox["i", "1"]], "\[CirclePlus]", 
      SubscriptBox["x", 
       SubscriptBox["i", "2"]], "\[CirclePlus]", "\[Ellipsis]", "\[CirclePlus]", 
      SubscriptBox["x", 
       SubscriptBox["i", "k"]]}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"acb556b0-5078-40aa-b6e4-2526ae3db5d1"],

Cell["\<\
A CNN built from convolutions + ReLU + MaxPool is therefore already a \
tropical rational map -- with no other operations involved.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0fe41e5f-a7f5-47c9-925a-1eea9394aaa0"],

Cell["\<\
MaxPool1D[x_List, k_Integer] :=
  Table[Max @@ x[[i ;; i + k - 1]], {i, 1, Length[x] - k + 1}];

MaxPool1D[{1, 3, 2, 7, 4, 5, 2, 8, 1}, 3]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"94515178-2c06-4b09-b67a-40b05abdbcf7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "7", ",", "7", ",", "7", ",", "5", ",", "8", ",", "8"}], 
   "}"}],
  Alignment->{Center, Top},
  ImageSize->Full]], "Output",
 CellFrame->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"63b46fad-9fb2-4a23-8d30-ce70b414442a"],

Cell["Hard tanh", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"10c8a86a-c2ea-45e1-8c62-bdfc02e7f9d4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<HardTanh\>\"", "(", "x", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{"min", "(", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", 
       RowBox[{"max", "(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "x"}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"0b419583-6892-443b-bc5b-a0198e919510"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Hard-tanh mixes a max-plus operation (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"\"\<Max\>\"", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "x"}], ")"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "df9a2d1b-6e10-457c-aedf-dbb283296283"],
 ") with a min-plus one (the outer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["Min",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "264f5e27-53d5-4d2a-b400-5182a24e3bfe"],
 "). Min-plus is just max-plus on the negated values, so the same algebra \
applies if we keep two parallel \"signs\" of the input. Practically: the \
analytical tools below (Lipschitz, dead units, pruning) still work on \
hard-tanh layers, but you need to track both upper and lower hulls, doubling \
the bookkeeping. The pure ReLU case is the cleanest entry point, which is \
what we will stick with."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ff6c21cc-2e70-424c-963b-2d84dd38b423"],

Cell["Maxout (Goodfellow et al., 2013)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"c9fca418-3401-412f-9920-2949e23dbb56"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A maxout unit computes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["Max",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a024eb41-b18d-4404-aec9-b1e8ad89cb21"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["k",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e43003cf-93e5-43af-b3f3-a6be5381a2b9"],
 " affine functions of its input:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e074b7b8-0eac-4015-b469-48d2da249333"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<MaxoutUnit\>\"", "(", "x", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["Max", "\"\<i = 1 .. k\>\""], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["w", "i"], ".", "x"}], "+", 
        SubscriptBox["b", "i"]}], ")"}]}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"c5793a7c-dffb-4303-ad6c-e6ccb1b057ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Equivalently, ",
 StyleBox["a maxout unit IS a tropical polynomial",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". The hidden layer of a maxout network is a vector of tropical polynomials, \
and the whole network is a tropical rational map by construction -- no \
decomposition needed, no positive/negative weight split. From the tropical \
standpoint, maxout is a more natural activation than ReLU."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"82b8f492-3e6e-40c7-862e-e7fbe2fb3397"],

Cell["\<\
MaxoutUnit[x_?VectorQ, W_?MatrixQ, biases_?VectorQ] :=
  Max @@ (W . x + biases);

W = {{1., 0.5}, {-1., 2.}, {0., -1.}};
b = {0.1, -0.2, 0.3};
MaxoutUnit[{1.0, 1.0}, W, b]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fad1e150-c281-48e4-9cd0-8b6b53a81a65"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox["1.6`",
  Alignment->{Center, Top},
  ImageSize->Full]], "Output",
 CellFrame->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"c72d794c-987a-4d53-bbde-b168c6ae8524"],

Cell["Skip connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3a497e67-a138-4238-9b70-ebce6aa4c23b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<ResBlock\>\"", "(", "x", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{"x", "+", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<F\>\"", "(", "x", ")"}]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{"x", "\[CircleTimes]", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<F\>\"", "(", "x", ")"}]}]}],
    HoldForm],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"17084f8d-12d3-4109-8a6f-80a7305625a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Classical addition is tropical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["CircleTimes",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "324d7e24-d415-4e18-bcbb-df94006f1cd4"],
 ", so a residual connection is just a tropical product. A ResNet of ReLU \
layers stays inside the tropical algebra."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"607280e5-c9af-4852-a261-88f1f66789b2"],

Cell["13.  Train a tiny classifier and verify", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"44474bce-4780-4b95-9935-ca0e5255a21b"],

Cell["The two-moons dataset", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"79b27abe-ad21-4f46-a09b-1b9e63e7f064"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before we touch a single neuron we have to pick a problem. ",
 StyleBox["Two-moons",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is the classic 2D toy classification dataset: two interlocking \
crescent-shaped point clouds in the plane, one labelled ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"+", "1"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6d20dcac-8d5e-4702-888c-80fd848b855a"],
 " and the other ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6d818252-8f22-4581-a391-80ef11e84048"],
 ", with a little Gaussian noise sprinkled on top. The two crescents cannot \
be separated by any straight line -- that is the entire point of the dataset. \
Any non-linear classifier worth its salt should be able to carve the plane \
cleanly between them, and the shape of the carve is interesting enough to \
make pretty pictures."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e48eb138-19d8-49a5-be78-0ae421b9f3f1"],

