Cell["\<\
Figure 3. Newton polytope of P (top row) and Q (bottom row) for the trained \
moons classifier. The 3D upper hull (left) and the linear-piece partition of \
input space (right) are dual: 4 of P's 7 monomials and 5 of Q's 7 monomials \
realise a region. The rest are dominated everywhere and contribute nothing -- \
exactly the kind of redundancy we are about to exploit in \[Section]18.\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"517d3e46-da1e-4950-aacf-9a58e52421bb"],

Cell["16.  Linear regions scale like n^2", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"91a483f6-9161-4e17-8c79-cfff8b39ebbf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What does \"more hidden units\" do to the function the network computes? \
Geometrically, each new unit cuts the input plane along one more straight \
crease and lets the surface fold along it. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["n",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1622dda7-257f-43d4-bb4e-bb53f8c40baa"],
 " creases, the surface acquires up to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox[
     RowBox[{"Order", "[", 
      SuperscriptBox["n", "2"], "]"}],
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5ea06a26-3528-493e-807b-1daa541dcb78"],
 " flat facets -- a number that, for large ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["n",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "739ce57d-bab4-4e9d-b5c0-c28ef9899946"],
 " grows much faster than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TagBox[
   FormBox[
    TagBox["n",
     HoldForm],
    TraditionalForm],
   TraditionalForm,
   Editable->True]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2221804c-0591-4472-a653-9defd97327ac"],
 " itself."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67d0af7f-3d68-4be3-8a66-a8bd1e385995"],

